			<item>
				<title>About the Photographer</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/portrait.jpg&#34; &#xA;alt=&#34;Alex Walker&#34; &#xA;style=&#34;float: left; width: 300px; margin-right: 40px; margin-bottom: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--border);&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p style=&#34;margin-top: 0;&#34;&gt;&#xA;   I&#39;m a photographer and naval architect based in New Hampshire. I&#39;ve lived in New England my whole life - from Connecticut to Maine.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;    My primary work, Eastern Americana, documents the functional remnants scattered across the New England landscape. I grew up learning to read these traces and now spend my time following old maps to forgotten sites, photographing what remains.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
